{{also|cutdown}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[cut]] [[down]]|cuts down|cutting down|cut down}}

# {{&lit|cut|down|lang=en}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To bring down by cutting.
#: ''They want to '''cut down''' several trees to make room for the parking lot.''
# {{context|idiomatic|transitive|lang=en}} To [[insult]], to [[belittle]].
# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[reduce]] the [[amount]] of something.
#: ''He wants to '''cut down''' on extra steps.''
#: ''Please don't put the candy jar right next to my desk. I'm trying to '''cut down''' on sugar.''
# {{context|idiomatic|dated|lang=en}} To [[slay]], often in great numbers.

====Usage notes====
* In all senses, the object may appear before or after the particle. If it is a pronoun, it MUST precede the particle.

